{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The ratio of particles that should actually be emitted. If set to a value lower than "},{"code":"1.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", this will set the amount of emitted particles throughout the lifetime to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"amount * amount_ratio"},{"text":". Unlike changing ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amount","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", changing "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amountRatio","isActive":true},{"text":" while emitting does not affect already-emitted particles and doesn’t cause the particle system to restart. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amountRatio","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" can be used to create effects that make the number of emitted particles vary over time."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"amountRatio"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducing the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GPUParticles2D\/amountRatio","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" has no performance benefit, since resources need to be allocated and processed for the 